## 🧪 Postman Test Data

### Test 1: Create Full Job (all nested data)
Use the full request body from API 1 above.

### Test 2: Create Minimal Job
```json
{
  "company_id": "<companyId>",
  "job_title": "Infosys Intern 2026",
  "job_location": "Pune",
  "job_type": "internship",
  "internship_duration": "6 months",
  "internship_stipend": "15000/month",
  "passout_year": 2026,
  "application_deadline": "2026-04-01T23:59:59Z",
  "positions": [
    { "position_name": "Intern — Development", "vacancies": 10 }
  ]
}
```

### Test 3: Inactive Company (expect 400)
Use a deactivated company's ID → `"Cannot create a job for an inactive company"`

### Test 4: Past Deadline (expect 400)
```json
{ "application_deadline": "2025-01-01T00:00:00Z", ... }
```

### Test 5: salary_min > salary_max (expect 400)
```json
{ "salary_min": 1000000, "salary_max": 500000, ... }
```

### Test 6: List All Jobs
```
GET /api/college/get_all_jobs?page=1&limit=20
```

### Test 7: Filter by Year + Status
```
GET /api/college/get_all_jobs?passout_year=2026&job_status=draft
```

### Test 8: Search Jobs
```
GET /api/college/get_all_jobs?search=tcs
```

### Test 9: Get Job Detail
```
GET /api/college/get_job/<jobId>
```

### Test 10: Update Job
```
PUT /api/college/update_job/<jobId>
```
```json
{ "salary_package": "8 LPA", "salary_max": 800000 }
```

### Test 11: Publish Job (draft → published)
```
PATCH /api/college/update_job_status/<jobId>
```
```json
{ "job_status": "published" }
```

### Test 12: Close Job (published → closed)
```json
{ "job_status": "closed" }
```

### Test 13: Reopen Job (closed → published)
```json
{ "job_status": "published" }
```

### Test 14: Cancel Job
```json
{ "job_status": "cancelled" }
```

### Test 15: Invalid Transition (cancelled → published, expect 400)
```json
{ "job_status": "published" }
```

